INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("TRIGGERS SCRIPTING SCRIPTS", "A trigger is a small script attached to a room, a mobile or an object. It runs\nwhen something happens to that thing: someone walks in, says a word, hands it\nan item, attacks it, or the clock reaches a certain hour.\n\nTriggers are written with ^gTRIGEDIT^n and live in zones, with vnums, like\nrooms and mobiles. Each one declares up front whether it is meant for a\nmobile, an object or a room, because the events it can listen for differ.\n\nTriggers cannot be attached to players.\n\n^WWhere to read next^n\n  ^cTRIGEDIT^n           writing, editing and saving a trigger\n  ^cMOB TRIGGERS^n       what makes a mobile\'s trigger fire\n  ^cOBJECT TRIGGERS^n    what makes an object\'s trigger fire\n  ^cROOM TRIGGERS^n      what makes a room\'s trigger fire\n  ^cSCRIPT COMMANDS^n    if, while, switch, wait, set, and the rest\n  ^cSCRIPT VARIABLES^n   %actor%, %self%, and how fields are read\n  ^cMOB COMMANDS^n       what a mobile\'s script can make it do\n  ^cOBJECT COMMANDS^n    what an object\'s script can make it do\n  ^cROOM COMMANDS^n      what a room\'s script can make it do\n  ^cZONE TRIGGERS^n      attaching a trigger on zone reset\n  ^cPLAYER VARIABLES^n   quest state that follows a player around\n  ^cTSTAT^n              inspecting triggers and variables in play\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGEDIT, TATTACH, TSTAT^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("TRIGEDIT", "Usage: ^gTRIGEDIT <vnum>^n\n\nOpens the trigger editor on a vnum in a zone you have build access to. If\nnothing exists there yet you get a blank trigger to fill in.\n\n  ^c1^n Name          A label for builders. Players never see it.\n  ^c2^n Intended for  Mobiles, objects or rooms. Changing this clears the\n                  trigger types, since they mean different things for each.\n  ^c3^n Trigger types Which events fire this trigger. Set at least one, or it\n                  can never run.\n  ^c4^n Numeric arg   Meaning depends on the type, and is usually a percent\n                  chance. See ^cMOB TRIGGERS^n, ^cOBJECT TRIGGERS^n and\n                  ^cROOM TRIGGERS^n for what each type does with it.\n  ^c5^n Arguments     The command word, the phrase, or the list of words the\n                  type matches on. Not every type uses it.\n  ^c6^n Commands      The script itself.\n  ^cw^n Copy another trigger over this one.\n  ^cq^n Quit and save.   ^cx^n Exit and abort.\n\nOption ^c6^n opens a blank page, and what you write there replaces the script\nthat was in it, so bring a copy of anything you mean to keep. Writing nothing\nat all leaves the old script alone. The script is re-indented for you when the\ntrigger is saved.\n\nSaving writes the trigger to disk straight away and updates every copy of it\nalready running in the world.\n\nTo make a trigger part of a room, mobile or object permanently, use the\n^cw) Attached triggers^n option in ^gREDIT^n, ^gMEDIT^n or ^gIEDIT^n. To hang one on a\nsingle thing until the next reboot, use ^gTATTACH^n.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TATTACH, TSTAT, SCRIPT COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("TATTACH TDETACH", "Usage: ^gTATTACH { mob | obj | room } { trigger } { name } [ location ]\n       TDETACH [ mob | object | room ] { target } { trigger | \'all\' }^n\n\n^gTATTACH^n puts a trigger onto one thing that is already in the world, by\ntrigger vnum. ^gTDETACH^n takes one off by vnum, or \'all\' to strip the lot.\n\nNeither is saved. They change the one mobile, object or room you named, not\nevery copy of it, and they last until the next reboot. For an attachment that\nsurvives, use the ^cw) Attached triggers^n option in ^gREDIT^n, ^gMEDIT^n or ^gIEDIT^n,\nor a zone ^cT^n command.\n\nA trigger written for a mobile will not attach to a room, and neither will\nattach to a player.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TRIGEDIT, TSTAT, ZONE TRIGGERS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("TSTAT VDELETE", "Usage: ^gTSTAT <vnum>\n       VDELETE { <variable name> | * | all } <id>^n\n\n^gTSTAT^n prints one trigger prototype: its name, what it is intended for, the\ntypes set on it, its numeric argument and arguments, and the script.\n\n^gSTAT^n on a room, mobile or object lists the triggers attached to that one\nthing and the variables stored on it. On a player it lists the variables. The\nid it prints is the script id, which is what ^gVDELETE^n wants.\n\n^gVDELETE^n removes a stored variable by name, or ^c*^n / ^call^n to remove every\nvariable, from whatever the id belongs to. On a player this also removes it\nfrom the saved character.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TRIGEDIT, PLAYER VARIABLES, SCRIPT VARIABLES^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"MOB TRIGGERS\" MTRIGGERS", "Trigger types for a mobile, with what the numeric argument means and the\nvariables the trigger starts with. Every trigger also has ^c%self%^n, the\nmobile it is attached to.\n\n^cGlobal^n     Not an event. Set it alongside Random or Time so the trigger is\n           still checked when the zone has nobody in it.\n^cRandom^n     Every few seconds. Arg is the percent chance per check.\n^cCommand^n    Someone in the room types a command. Arguments is the command\n           word, or ^c*^n for any command. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%cmd%^n, ^c%arg%^n.\n           The command is swallowed unless the script does ^creturn 0^n, which\n           lets it run normally.\n^cSpeech^n     Someone in the room speaks. Arguments is the text to look for.\n           Arg 0 matches it anywhere in the sentence; any other value matches\n           whole words only. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%speech%^n.\n^cAct^n        Something is echoed into the room. Matching works as for Speech.\n           Sets ^c%actor%^n and, where the message had them, ^c%victim%^n,\n           ^c%object%^n, ^c%target%^n, ^c%arg%^n.\n^cDeath^n      The mobile dies. Arg is the percent chance. ^c%actor%^n is not\n           set: by the time the game gets here it no longer has hold of\n           whoever landed the blow.\n^cGreet^n      Someone has entered the room and the mobile can see them. Arg\n           is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n and ^c%direction%^n, the way\n           they came from. The move has already happened by this point, so\n           ^creturn 0^n does not turn them back; it only stops the rest of the\n           room\'s greet triggers from running.\n^cGreet-All^n  As Greet, but fires whether or not the mobile can see them.\n^cEntry^n      The mobile itself walks into a room. Arg is the percent chance.\n^cReceive^n    Someone gives the mobile an object. Arg is the percent chance.\n           Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%object%^n. ^creturn 0^n refuses the object.\n^cFight^n      Every combat round while the mobile is fighting. Arg is the\n           percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n, its opponent.\n^cHitPrcnt^n   A combat round where the mobile\'s physical condition has fallen\n           to arg percent or below. Sets ^c%actor%^n.\n^cBribe^n      Someone gives the mobile nuyen. Arg is the smallest amount that\n           will fire it. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%amount%^n.\n^cLoad^n       The mobile is loaded by a zone reset, by ^gWIZLOAD^n, or by another\n           script. Arg is the percent chance. Mobiles conjured by other game\n           systems, such as spirits and elementals, do not fire it.\n^cMemory^n     Someone the mobile has been told to remember walks in. Arg is\n           the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n. See ^cMOB COMMANDS^n for\n           ^gMREMEMBER^n.\n^cCast^n       Someone in the room casts a spell at the mobile. Arg is the\n           percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%spell%^n, ^c%spellname%^n.\n^cLeave^n      Someone tries to leave the room. Arg is the percent chance.\n           Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%direction%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cDoor^n       Someone opens, closes, locks, unlocks or picks a door in the\n           room. Arg is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%cmd%^n,\n           ^c%direction%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cDamage^n     The mobile takes damage. Arg is the percent chance. Sets\n           ^c%actor%^n, ^c%victim%^n, ^c%damdealt%^n, ^c%attacktype%^n.\n^cTime^n       Arg is the game hour, 0 to 23, at which it fires.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TRIGEDIT, MOB COMMANDS, SCRIPT VARIABLES^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"OBJECT TRIGGERS\" OTRIGGERS", "Trigger types for an object, with what the numeric argument means and the\nvariables the trigger starts with. Every trigger also has ^c%self%^n, the object\nit is attached to.\n\n^cRandom^n   Every few seconds, while the object is somewhere a script can see\n         it. Arg is the percent chance per check.\n^cCommand^n  Someone in the same room as the object, or carrying it, types a\n         command. Arguments is the command word, or ^c*^n for any command.\n         Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%cmd%^n, ^c%arg%^n. The command is swallowed unless the\n         script does ^creturn 0^n.\n^cTimer^n    The object\'s timer runs out. No percent chance; it always fires.\n^cGet^n      Someone picks the object up. Arg is the percent chance. Sets\n         ^c%actor%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cDrop^n     Someone drops it. Arg is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n.\n         ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cGive^n     Someone gives it away. Arg is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n\n         and ^c%victim%^n, the recipient. ^creturn 0^n stops the handover.\n^cWear^n     Someone wears or wields it. Always fires. Sets ^c%actor%^n.\n         ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cRemove^n   Someone takes it off. Always fires. Sets ^c%actor%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops\n         them.\n^cLoad^n     The object is loaded by a zone reset, by ^gWIZLOAD^n, or by another\n         script. Arg is the percent chance. Objects created by other game\n         systems do not fire it.\n^cCast^n     Someone casts a spell at the object. Arg is the percent chance.\n         Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%spell%^n, ^c%spellname%^n.\n^cLeave^n    Someone tries to leave the room the object is lying in. Arg is\n         the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%direction%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops\n         them.\n^cConsume^n  Someone eats, drinks from or quaffs it. Arg picks which: 1 for\n         eating, 2 for drinking, 3 for all three. Sets ^c%actor%^n and\n         ^c%command%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cTime^n     Arg is the game hour, 0 to 23, at which it fires.\n\nThe ^cGlobal^n type is listed for objects but has no effect on them.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TRIGEDIT, OBJECT COMMANDS, SCRIPT VARIABLES^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"ROOM TRIGGERS\" WTRIGGERS", "Trigger types for a room, with what the numeric argument means and the\nvariables the trigger starts with. Every trigger also has ^c%self%^n, the room it\nis attached to.\n\n^cGlobal^n   Not an event. Set it alongside Random or Time so the trigger is\n         still checked when the zone has nobody in it.\n^cRandom^n   Every few seconds. Arg is the percent chance per check.\n^cCommand^n  Someone in the room types a command. Arguments is the command\n         word, or ^c*^n for any command. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%cmd%^n, ^c%arg%^n. The\n         command is swallowed unless the script does ^creturn 0^n. Room command\n         triggers are checked before mobile and object ones.\n^cSpeech^n   Someone in the room speaks. Arguments is the text to look for.\n         Arg 0 matches it anywhere in the sentence; any other value matches\n         whole words only. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%speech%^n.\n^cReset^n    The room\'s zone resets. Arg is the percent chance.\n^cEnter^n    Someone has walked in. Arg is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n\n         and ^c%direction%^n, the way they came from. The move has already\n         happened, so ^creturn 0^n does not turn them back; it only stops the\n         mobile triggers that would otherwise run next. To refuse a move,\n         use a ^cLeave^n trigger on the room they are coming from.\n^cDrop^n     Someone drops something in the room. Arg is the percent chance.\n         Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%object%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cCast^n     Someone casts a spell in the room. Arg is the percent chance.\n         Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%spell%^n, ^c%spellname%^n, and where the spell had them,\n         ^c%victim%^n and ^c%object%^n.\n^cLeave^n    Someone tries to leave. Arg is the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n,\n         ^c%direction%^n. ^creturn 0^n stops them.\n^cDoor^n     Someone opens, closes, locks, unlocks or picks a door here. Arg is\n         the percent chance. Sets ^c%actor%^n, ^c%cmd%^n, ^c%direction%^n. ^creturn 0^n\n         stops them.\n^cLogin^n    A player connects in this room. Arg is the percent chance. Sets\n         ^c%actor%^n.\n^cTime^n     Arg is the game hour, 0 to 23, at which it fires.\n\nSomeone riding in a vehicle is not standing in the room, so no room trigger\nwill see them.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TRIGEDIT, ROOM COMMANDS, SCRIPT VARIABLES^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"SCRIPT COMMANDS\" \"SCRIPT SYNTAX\"", "A script is a list of lines. Anything that is not one of the words below is\nhanded to the mobile, object or room as a command. Lines beginning with ^c*^n are\ncomments.\n\n^WFlow^n\n  ^cif <expression>^n / ^celseif <expression>^n / ^celse^n / ^cend^n\n  ^cwhile <expression>^n / ^cdone^n\n  ^cswitch <expression>^n / ^ccase <value>^n / ^cdefault^n / ^cbreak^n / ^cdone^n\n  ^cbreak^n also leaves a while loop.\n  ^chalt^n              Stop the script here.\n  ^creturn 0^n / ^creturn 1^n  Tell the game whether to let the interrupted action\n                    go ahead. Which types listen is noted in ^cMOB TRIGGERS^n,\n                    ^cOBJECT TRIGGERS^n and ^cROOM TRIGGERS^n. The default is 1.\n  ^cnop <expression>^n  Evaluate something and throw the answer away. Useful\n                    for fields that act when you read them, such as\n                    ^c%actor.skillset(pistols 4)%^n.\n\nAn expression compares two values with ^c==^n ^c!=^n ^c<^n ^c>^n ^c<=^n ^c>=^n, tests\nsubstrings with ^c/=^n, combines with ^c&&^n and ^c||^n, and does arithmetic with\n^c+^n ^c-^n ^c*^n ^c/^n. A bare value is true if it is a non-zero number or a\nnon-empty string.\n\n^WVariables^n\n  ^cset <name> <value>^n     Make or change a variable in this script.\n  ^ceval <name> <expr>^n     As set, but works the expression out first.\n  ^cunset <name>^n           Forget it.\n  ^cglobal <name>^n          Keep it on the mobile, object or room running the\n                          script, so later triggers on that thing see it.\n  ^ccontext <number>^n       Namespace the globals, so several copies of the\n                          same script do not tread on each other.\n  ^cremote <name> <id>^n     Copy a variable onto whatever has that script id.\n  ^crdelete <name> <id>^n    Remove one from there again.\n\n^WOther^n\n  ^cwait <n> sec^n / ^cwait <n>^n   Pause. The script resumes where it left off, so\n                          check that everyone involved is still there.\n  ^cwait until <hh:mm>^n     Pause until that game time.\n  ^cattach <vnum> <id>^n     Put another trigger on something at run time.\n  ^cdetach <vnum> <id>^n     Take one off again.\n  ^cextract <name> <n> <text>^n  Put the nth word of the text into a variable.\n  ^cmakeuid <name> <id>^n\n  ^cmakeuid <name> mob|obj|room <what>^n\n                          Make a variable that points at something, so it can\n                          be used as ^c%name%^n and have fields read off it.\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT VARIABLES, TRIGEDIT, PLAYER VARIABLES^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"SCRIPT VARIABLES\"", "A script writes ^c%name%^n to have the value put in. If what it names is a\ncharacter, an object or a room, a field can be read off it with a dot, and\nsome fields take an argument in brackets:\n\n  ^c%actor.name%^n   ^c%self.vnum%^n   ^c%actor.eq(WIELD)%^n   ^c%self.val0%^n\n\n^WWhat you start with^n\n  ^c%self%^n    the mobile, object or room the trigger is attached to\n  ^c%actor%^n   whoever set the trigger off, where there is one\n  Other names depend on the type: see ^cMOB TRIGGERS^n, ^cOBJECT TRIGGERS^n and\n  ^cROOM TRIGGERS^n.\n\n^WLooking things up^n\n  ^c%global.<name>%^n           A variable shared by every script on the game.\n                             Write one with ^cremote <name> %global%^n.\n  ^c%people.<room vnum>%^n      How many people are in that room.\n  ^c%time.hour%^n, ^c%time.day%^n, ^c%time.month%^n, ^c%time.year%^n\n  ^c%findmob.<room>(<vnum>)%^n  How many of that mobile are in that room.\n  ^c%findobj.<room>(<x>)%^n     How many objects of that vnum or name are\n                             lying in that room.\n  ^c%random.<n>%^n              A number from 1 to n.\n  ^c%random.char%^n             Someone at random in the room. A mobile will\n                             not pick itself, or anyone it cannot see.\n  ^c%random.dir%^n              A random direction.\n\n^WField lists^n\n  ^cCHARACTER FIELDS^n   what you can read off a person\n  ^cOBJECT FIELDS^n      what you can read off an object\n  ^cROOM FIELDS^n        what you can read off a room\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT COMMANDS, PLAYER VARIABLES, TRIGGERS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"CHARACTER FIELDS\"", "Fields for a character, as in ^c%actor.name%^n. Some take an argument in\nbrackets, and a few change the character when given one.\n\n^WWho they are^n\n  ^cname^n ^ctitle^n ^cid^n ^cvnum^n ^clevel^n ^cis_pc^n ^csex^n ^cpronouns^n\n  ^cheshe^n ^chimher^n ^chisher^n ^cheight^n ^cweight^n ^ccanbeseen^n\n  ^cvnum(<vnum>)^n is 1 if the mobile is that vnum.\n\n^WAttributes^n\n  ^cbod^n ^cqui^n ^cstr^n ^ccha^n ^cint^n ^cwil^n ^cmag^n ^crea^n ^cess^n\n  ^ccon^n, ^cdex^n and ^cwis^n are accepted as other names for ^cbod^n, ^cqui^n and\n  ^cwil^n.\n\n^WCondition and resources^n\n  ^cphysical^n ^cmaxphysical^n   physical condition monitor, in boxes\n  ^cmental^n ^cmaxmental^n       mental condition monitor, in boxes\n  ^chitp^n ^cmaxhitp^n           other names for the physical monitor\n  ^cmana^n ^cmaxmana^n           other names for the mental monitor\n  ^cnuyen^n ^cgold^n             nuyen on hand\n  ^ckarma^n ^cexp^n              karma\n  ^carmor^n ^cballistic^n ^cimpact^n\n  Given a number, ^cphysical^n, ^cmental^n, ^cnuyen^n and ^ckarma^n add it.\n\n^WSkills^n\n  ^cskill(<name>)^n              that skill\'s rating, or \'unknown skill\'\n  ^cskillset(<name> <rating>)^n  set a player\'s skill. Read it with ^cnop^n.\n\n^WPosition, state and flags^n\n  ^cpos^n            the position by name; give one to change it\n  ^cfighting^n       who they are fighting\n  ^cmaster^n         who they are following\n  ^cfollower^n       their first follower\n  ^cnpcflag(<flag>)^n   1 if that mobile flag is set\n  ^cpref(<flag>)^n      1 if that player preference is set\n  ^cquest^n          the player\'s current quest number, or 0\n\n^WWhere they are and what they carry^n\n  ^croom^n              the room they are in\n  ^cnext_in_room^n      the next person in the room, for walking the list\n  ^cinventory^n         their first carried object, or ^cinventory(<vnum>)^n for\n                     one of that vnum\n  ^ceq(<position>)^n    what is worn there. Positions are the short names, for\n                     example ^cHEAD^n, ^cBODY^n, ^cWIELD^n, ^cABOUT^n, ^cFEET^n.\n                     ^ceq(*)^n is 1 if they are wearing anything at all.\n  ^chas_item(<vnum>)^n  1 if they are carrying one\n\n^WScripts^n\n  ^cvarexists(<name>)^n  1 if a variable of that name is stored on them\n  ^chasattached(<vnum>)^n  1 if that trigger is attached\n  ^calias^n             the mobile\'s keywords\n  ^cglobal(<name>)^n     a variable stored on a mobile by ^cglobal^n\n\nAny name that is not a field is looked up as a variable stored on that\ncharacter, so ^c%actor.mytally%^n reads back what ^cremote^n put there.\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT VARIABLES, OBJECT FIELDS, ROOM FIELDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"OBJECT FIELDS\"", "Fields for an object, as in ^c%self.shortdesc%^n.\n\n  ^cname^n            the object\'s keywords\n  ^cshortdesc^n       the short description\n  ^cvnum^n            its vnum, or ^cvnum(<vnum>)^n to test for one\n  ^cid^n              its script id\n  ^ctype^n            the item type by name\n  ^ccost^n ^cweight^n     give ^cweight^n a number to change it\n  ^cval0^n to ^cval17^n   the object\'s values. Change one with ^gOSETVAL^n.\n  ^ctimer^n           the object\'s timer; give a number to set it\n  ^cextra(<flag>)^n   1 if that extra flag is set; with no argument, the list\n  ^cwearflag(<pos>)^n 1 if it can be worn there\n  ^caffects^n         the affects on it\n  ^cis_pc^n           always -1, so a script can tell an object from a person\n\n^WWhere it is^n\n  ^ccarried_by^n      who is carrying it\n  ^cworn_by^n         who is wearing it\n  ^croom^n            the room it is in, wherever it is being kept\n  ^cis_inroom^n       the room, but only if it is lying on the floor\n  ^cnext_in_list^n    the next object beside it, for walking a list\n  ^ccontents^n        the first object inside it, or ^ccontents(<vnum>)^n\n\n^WContainers^n\n  ^chas_in(<x>)^n     1 if a container holds one\n  ^ccount(<x>)^n      how many a container holds\n\n^WScripts^n\n  ^chasattached(<vnum>)^n  1 if that trigger is attached\n\nAny name that is not a field is looked up as a variable stored on the object,\nso ^c%self.lastloaded%^n reads back what ^gOLOAD^n put there.\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT VARIABLES, CHARACTER FIELDS, ROOM FIELDS, OBJECT COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"ROOM FIELDS\"", "Fields for a room, as in ^c%self.name%^n.\n\n  ^cname^n         the room title\n  ^cvnum^n         its vnum, or ^cvnum(<vnum>)^n to test for one\n  ^cid^n           its script id\n  ^csector^n       the sector type by name\n  ^croomflag(<flag>)^n  1 if that room flag is set\n  ^czonenumber^n   the vnum of the zone it belongs to\n  ^czonename^n     that zone\'s name\n  ^cweather^n      sunny, cloudy, rainy or lightning outdoors; nothing inside\n  ^cpeople^n       the first person in the room, for walking the list with\n               ^cnext_in_room^n\n  ^ccontents^n     the first object on the floor, or ^ccontents(<vnum>)^n\n  ^chasattached(<vnum>)^n  1 if that trigger is attached\n\nAn exit is read by direction: ^c%self.north%^n gives that exit\'s flags, and is\nempty if there is no exit that way. The subfields are ^c%self.north(room)%^n,\n^c%self.north(vnum)%^n, ^c%self.north(key)%^n and ^c%self.north(barrier)%^n.\n\nAny name that is not a field is looked up as a variable stored on the room.\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT VARIABLES, CHARACTER FIELDS, OBJECT FIELDS, ROOM COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"MOB COMMANDS\" MCOMMANDS", "A mobile\'s script can use these as well as anything the mobile could type. A\ntarget may be a name in the room, or a ^c%variable%^n holding a script id.\n\n  ^cmsend <target> <text>^n        say something to one person\n  ^cmechoaround <target> <text>^n  to everyone in the room but that person\n  ^cmecho <text>^n                 to the whole room\n  ^cmrecho <from> <to> <text>^n    to every room in that vnum range\n  ^cmasound <text>^n               to every room next door\n  ^cmzoneecho <room> <text>^n      to every room in that room\'s zone\n  ^cmat <room> <command>^n         do something as if standing in that room\n  ^cmgoto <room>^n                 move the mobile there quietly\n  ^cmteleport <target> <room>^n    move someone else there. ^call^n moves everyone\n                                in the mobile\'s room.\n  ^cmforce <target> <command>^n    make someone do something. ^call^n forces\n                                everyone in the room.\n  ^cmkill <target>^n               attack\n  ^cmdamage <target> <boxes>^n     deal that many boxes of physical damage; a\n                                negative number heals. Capped at Deadly, and\n                                staff are not harmed.\n  ^cmhunt <target>^n               start hunting someone\n  ^cmfollow <target>^n             start following someone\n  ^cmremember <target>^n           remember someone, for a Memory trigger\n  ^cmforget <target>^n             stop remembering them\n  ^cmload mob <vnum> [room]^n\n  ^cmload obj <vnum> [target [position]]^n\n                                Load a mobile or an object. A mobile appears\n                                in the given room, or beside this one. An\n                                object goes to the named person or container,\n                                worn at ^cposition^n if one is given, and\n                                otherwise to the mobile itself. Either way its\n                                script id lands in ^c%self.lastloaded%^n.\n  ^cmjunk <object>^n               destroy something the mobile is carrying;\n                                ^call^n destroys the lot\n  ^cmpurge [target]^n              destroy something in the room, or the mobile\n                                itself with ^cmpurge self^n. The script finishes\n                                first.\n  ^cmtransform <vnum>^n            become a different mobile, keeping what it\n                                is carrying, its condition, and any running\n                                scripts. ^cmtransform -<vnum>^n takes the new\n                                mobile\'s condition instead.\n  ^cmdoor <room> <dir> <field> [value]^n  change an exit. The field is one of\n                                ^cpurge^n, ^cdescription^n, ^cflags^n, ^ckey^n, ^cname^n\n                                or ^croom^n.\n  ^cmlog <text>^n                  write a line to the script log\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT COMMANDS, MOB TRIGGERS, OBJECT COMMANDS, ROOM COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"OBJECT COMMANDS\" OCOMMANDS", "An object\'s script can use these. Where a room is wanted the object\'s own\nroom is used if you leave it out.\n\n  ^cosend <target> <text>^n        say something to one person\n  ^coechoaround <target> <text>^n  to everyone in the room but that person\n  ^coecho <text>^n                 to the room the object is in\n  ^corecho <from> <to> <text>^n    to every room in that vnum range\n  ^coasound <text>^n               to every room next door\n  ^cozoneecho <room> <text>^n      to every room in that room\'s zone\n  ^coat <room> <command>^n         do something as if the object were there\n  ^comove <room>^n                 move the object to that room\n  ^coteleport <target> <room>^n    move someone to that room. ^call^n moves\n                                everyone in the object\'s room.\n  ^coforce <target> <command>^n    make someone do something. ^call^n forces\n                                everyone in the room.\n  ^codamage <target> <boxes>^n     deal that many boxes of physical damage; a\n                                negative number heals\n  ^coload mob <vnum> [room]^n\n  ^coload obj <vnum> [target [position]]^n\n                                Load a mobile or an object. An object with no\n                                target is left in the object\'s own room. Its\n                                script id lands in ^c%self.lastloaded%^n.\n  ^copurge [target]^n              destroy something in the room, or the object\n                                itself with ^copurge self^n. The script finishes\n                                first.\n  ^cosetval <position> <value>^n   change one of the object\'s values, 0 to 17\n  ^cotimer <value>^n               set the object\'s timer\n  ^cotransform <vnum>^n            become a different object, keeping what is\n                                inside it and any running scripts\n  ^codoor <room> <dir> <field> [value]^n  change an exit. The field is one of\n                                ^cpurge^n, ^cdescription^n, ^cflags^n, ^ckey^n, ^cname^n\n                                or ^croom^n.\n  ^colog <text>^n                  write a line to the script log\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT COMMANDS, OBJECT TRIGGERS, OBJECT FIELDS, MOB COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"ROOM COMMANDS\" WCOMMANDS", "A room\'s script can use these. Where a room is wanted the room running the\nscript is used if you leave it out.\n\n  ^cwsend <target> <text>^n        say something to one person\n  ^cwechoaround <target> <text>^n  to everyone in the room but that person\n  ^cwecho <text>^n                 to the room\n  ^cwrecho <from> <to> <text>^n    to every room in that vnum range\n  ^cwasound <text>^n               to every room next door\n  ^cwzoneecho <room> <text>^n      to every room in that room\'s zone\n  ^cwat <room> <command>^n         do something as if in that room\n  ^cwmove <object> <room>^n        move an object lying here to that room\n  ^cwteleport <target> <room>^n    move someone there. ^call^n moves everyone in\n                                the room.\n  ^cwforce <target> <command>^n    make someone do something. ^call^n forces\n                                everyone in the room.\n  ^cwdamage <target> <boxes>^n     deal that many boxes of physical damage; a\n                                negative number heals\n  ^cwload mob <vnum>^n\n  ^cwload obj <vnum> [target [position]]^n\n                                Load a mobile or an object here. An object\n                                with no target is left on the floor. Its\n                                script id lands in ^c%self.lastloaded%^n.\n  ^cwpurge [target]^n              destroy something in the room\n  ^cwdoor <room> <dir> <field> [value]^n  change an exit. The field is one of\n                                ^cpurge^n, ^cdescription^n, ^cflags^n, ^ckey^n, ^cname^n\n                                or ^croom^n.\n  ^cwlog <text>^n                  write a line to the script log\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT COMMANDS, ROOM TRIGGERS, ROOM FIELDS, MOB COMMANDS^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"ZONE TRIGGERS\"", "A zone can attach a trigger when it resets, which is how a trigger gets onto\na mobile or object the zone has just loaded.\n\n  ^gT <if-flag> <attach type> <trigger vnum> <target vnum>^n\n\nThe attach type is ^c0^n for a mobile, ^c1^n for an object and ^c2^n for a room.\nFor types 0 and 1 the if-flag works as it does for the other zone commands, so\n^c1^n means \'only if the previous command succeeded\', which is what you want\nafter an ^cM^n or ^cO^n line: the trigger then lands on the thing that line just\nloaded, and the target vnum is ignored. For a room, the target vnum names the\nroom.\n\nTrigger vnums here are written as vnums and stay that way, so inserting a new\ntrigger does not disturb zone commands that already exist.\n\n^gZEDIT^n has no option for adding a ^cT^n line, so one has to be written into the\nzone file by hand. Once it is there the game keeps it: the boot rewrite puts\nit back out unchanged.\n\nAttaching a trigger in ^gREDIT^n, ^gMEDIT^n or ^gIEDIT^n puts it on every copy of that\nroom, mobile or object, which is usually what you want. A zone ^cT^n command is\nfor the cases where it is not.\n\n^WSee Also: TRIGGERS, TATTACH, TRIGEDIT^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
INSERT INTO help_topic (name, body) VALUES ("\"PLAYER VARIABLES\"", "A script can store a variable on a player and read it back later, which is how\nquest state follows someone around:\n\n  ^cremote tries %actor.id%^n         write the script\'s own \'tries\' onto them\n  ^cif %actor.tries% > 3^n            read it back, in this or any other script\n  ^crdelete tries %actor.id%^n        remove it again\n\nVariables stored on a player are saved with the character and are still there\nafter a reboot. Everything else a script stores is lost when the mobile,\nobject or room goes away.\n\nGive variables names that say which quest they belong to. Every script that\ntouches that player sees the same set.\n\nA player carries at most 128 of them. Changing one they already have is always\nallowed, so only new names can push against the limit; a refusal is written to\nthe script log with the trigger, the player and the name, so a runaway loop can\nbe found.\n\n^gSTAT^n on a player lists their variables, and ^gVDELETE^n removes one by hand.\n\n^WSee Also: SCRIPT COMMANDS, SCRIPT VARIABLES, TSTAT^n")  ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE  `name` = VALUES(`name`),  `body` = VALUES(`body`);
